Investigating the single tunnelling scale D_0^2 ~ Delta_1 and exact mode-by-mode matrix elements.

==========================================================================================================
PART 1: THE UNIFIED TUNNELLING SCALE & COMMUTATOR PROJECTION IDENTITY
==========================================================================================================
Testing the Exact Commutator Projection Identity:
    Delta_1 * <e_1, K c> = -D_0 * a_1   <===>   <e_1, K c> = - (D_0 * a_1) / Delta_1
and tracking the stability of the ratios R_D = D_0 / sqrt(Delta_1) and C_N = |a_1| / sqrt(Delta_1):

   N              D_0    sqrt(Delta_1)  R_D=D_0/sqrt(D)  C_N=|a_1|/sqrt(D)       <e_1, K c> -(D_0 a_1)/Delta_1   Identity Error
