  20    8.3835218e-19    1.3177851e-18        0.6361828           2.039563       -1.2975348         -1.2975348      1.27024e-15
  24     1.137963e-20    2.0845324e-20         0.545908           2.405934       -1.3134189         -1.3134189      1.56712e-12
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Finding Part 1:
1. Exact Identity Verified: |<e_1, Kc> + (D_0 a_1)/Delta_1| < 10^-50 across all dimensions!
2. The Single Tunnelling Scale: Both D_0 and sqrt(Delta_1) collapse by 10 decimal orders
   (8.05e-11 -> 1.14e-20), while their ratio R_D = D_0 / sqrt(Delta_1) remains strictly
   bounded in [0.41, 0.64] across the entire range.
3. Consequently, |a_1| / sqrt(Delta_1) = |<e_1, Kc>| / R_D remains stable in [1.97, 2.76].

