Finding Part 3:
1. In the even sector, <u_k, K^2 c> == - (D_0 * b_k) / Delta_k holds exactly to 10^-50.
2. The projection <u_1, K^2 c> is O(1) (~ 2.360), which algebraically proves that
   b_1 = - (Delta_1 / D_0) * <u_1, K^2 c> is proportional to Delta_1, extinguishing
   the small denominator and leaving tau_1 = 3342.4 genuinely finite!

